OL,3,GNEWSASignalman retires after 38 years
OL,4,Aat Britain's most unusual rail bridge
OL,5,
OL,6,FMick Brooks was a teenager the first
OL,7,Ftime his father took him to see the
OL,8,Fsliding bridge at Keadby. From that
OL,9,Fmoment, a love for life on the railway
OL,10,Fwas born.
OL,12,F"I fell for it and I always had
OL,13,Fintentions of getting here one day.
OL,14,FIt's my dad that set me off on the path
OL,15,Fof railways," he says.
OL,17,FHe didn't know then he'd retire from
OL,18,Fthe industry having spent 38 years
OL,19,Fworking at the place that first
OL,20,Finspired him - and watching over one of
OL,21,FBritain's most unusual rail crossings.
OL,23,APub: 24-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
